llvm-rc (used by clang-cl+lld-link cross builds, e.g. cmake/xwin-toolchain.cmake) fails to
parse a non-ASCII byte inside a VERSIONINFO string regardless of the declared/forced
codepage - it errors on this file's UTF-8 "\xc2\xa9" (c) even with --codepage=65001, which is
what the file's own `#pragma code_page(65001)` already requests. Confirmed against llvm-rc
20 and 21: dropping the character is what actually gets a complete .res out the other end
(370 bytes of truncated resource data on failure vs. 716 bytes once patched), not a codepage
flag. Real link.exe/rc.exe read this file fine as-is; this only matters cross-compiling.
--- a/res/d3d8to9.rc
+++ b/res/d3d8to9.rc
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
             VALUE "CompanyName", "crosire"
             VALUE "FileDescription", "d3d8to9"
             VALUE "FileVersion", "1.13.0.0"
-            VALUE "LegalCopyright", "Copyright © 2015. All rights reserved."
+            VALUE "LegalCopyright", "Copyright (c) 2015. All rights reserved."
             VALUE "OriginalFilename", "d3d8.dll"
             VALUE "ProductName", "ReShade"
             VALUE "ProductVersion", "3.0.0"
